UID:ms-medicaid-work-rule-2027@civic-forecast.pages.dev
DTSTAMP:20261027T020342Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270102
SUMMARY:Medicaid work rules begin by Jan. 1
DESCRIPTION:States must start requiring many adults ages 19 to 64 in the M
 edicaid expansion group to show 80 hours a month of work\, volunteering\,
  school or a work program. Many people are exempt\, such as parents of yo
 ung children and people who are medically frail. If you are on Medicaid\,
  watch for a letter from your state and ask the state agency whether this
  applies to you.\nMore: https://www.cms.gov/newsroom/fact-sheets/medicaid
 -community-engagement-requirement-certain-individuals-interim-final-rule-
 comment-period-cms\nFrom The Civic Forecast: https://civic-forecast.pages
 .dev
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://www.cms.gov/newsroom/fact-sheets/medicaid-community-engagement
 -requirement-certain-individuals-interim-final-rule-comment-period-cms
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Medicaid work rules begin by Jan. 1
TRIGGER:-PT15H
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
